 start of msg_size. msg[32] (OOB index 32) reads from 0x4160 = first element of msg_size array.\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F014\",\"type\":\"DERIVED\",\"description\":\"scanf %llu stores unsigned 64-bit value; JL compares as signed. Values with bit 63 set (>= 0x8000000000000000) are negative as signed and will pass idx < cookie_num (which is small positive), enabling negative/OOB array indexing.\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"}],\"uncertainties\":[{\"id\":\"U001\",\"description\":\"Whether OOB index in edit_cookie/read_cookie can reach useful targets (e.g., msg_size elements, urandom, cookie_num, or other BSS objects) for S2 to analyze\",\"reason\":\"Derived from layout: msg[-N] / msg[+OOB] addresses need S2 to compute exact reachable targets and assess exploitability\"},{\"id\":\"U002\",\"description\":\"Whether eat_cookie's swap-with-last without nulling creates a exploitable UAF/double-free primitive\",\"reason\":\"S2 needs to analyze the exact allocation/free sequence and whether the dangling pointer at msg[cookie_num-1] can be reused\"},{\"id\":\"U003\",\"description\":\"Runtime heap layout and tcache behavior under glibc 2.39\",\"reason\":\"S2/S3 need dynamic analysis to determine heap chunk placement and free-list behavior\"},{\"id\":\"U004\",\"description\":\"Whether msg_size[index]-1 can underflow when msg_size[index]==0 (OOB case reading 0 from adjacent memory)\",\"reason\":\"sub eax,0x1 on 0 gives -1, movsxd gives 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF as read size — S2 should analyze this path\"}],\"raw\":{\"elf\":\"ELF64 LSB PIE, x86-64, dynamically linked, interpreter /lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2, not stripped, BuildID=84dab319bf6fe22134cf0338cbd8071fd8bc06c2, GCC 10.2.0 (Debian)\",\"sections\":\".text@0x1110 RX 0x891 | .rodata@0x2000 R 0x266 | .data@0x4000 RW 0x10 | .bss@0x4020 RW 0x1d0 | .got@0x3f58 RW 0xa8 | .plt@0x1020 RX 0xe0 | .init_array@0x3d58 RW 8 | .fini_array@0x3d60 RW 8\",\"symbols\":\"main@0x187f | init@0x1232 | create_cookie@0x1399 | eat_cookie@0x14e1 | edit_cookie@0x1628 | read_cookie@0x1751 | menu@0x17fd | _abort@0x11f5 | msg@0x4060(256B) | msg_size@0x4160(128B) | cookie_num@0x41e8(8B) | urandom@0x41e0(8B)\",\"disassembly\":\"edit_cookie: scanf(%llu)->idx; cmp rdx,cookie_num; jl ok; (no lower bound); read(0,msg[idx],msg_size[idx]-1). read_cookie: same idx check; printf(%s,msg[idx]). eat_cookie: rand=fread(urandom)%cookie_num; free(msg[rand]); msg[rand]=msg[cookie_num-1]; msg_size[rand]=msg_size[cookie_num-1]; cookie_num--; (msg[cookie_num-1] not zeroed). create_cookie: if(cookie_num>0x1f)abort; scanf(%lld)->size; if(size>0x100)abort; calloc(size,1); read(0,buf,size); msg[cookie_num]=buf; msg_size[cookie_num]=size; cookie_num++.\"}},\"vulnerability_report\":null,\"primitive_reports\":[],\"target_bug\":\"\",\"bug_reports\":[],\"impact_reports\":[],\"strategy_reports\":[],\"final_exploit_path\":\"\",\"final_report\":{}}",
